{# Public safety notice band for the Today board.

   Renders nothing at all when no notice is live, so it is safe to leave in
   place permanently — the whole block disappears from the HTML rather than
   collapsing to an empty box.

   Deliberately NOT styled as an alarm. This is a town noticeboard, not an
   emergency broadcast: a calm bordered band that says what to look for and
   what to do. Red banners and warning triangles either frighten an older
   readership or train everyone to ignore banners, and both are worse than
   plain. The <h2> is sized DOWN from the page <h1>: a notice is important
   but it is not the identity of the page, and a heading larger than the
   page title inverts the document outline for screen reader users too.

   The link goes to the item in the register, so the notice is always
   traceable to the meeting where it was raised. #}

{% set live = notice.notices | currentNotices %}
{% for n in live %}
<section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="notice-h">
  <div class="notice-band">
    <p class="notice-kicker">Public safety notice</p>
    <h2 class="notice-title" id="notice-h">{{ n.title }}</h2>
    <p class="notice-body">{{ n.body }}</p>
    {% if n.sourceUrl %}
    <p class="notice-source"><a href="{{ n.sourceUrl }}">Where this came from →</a></p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}
